---
import '@fontsource/della-respira';
import '@fontsource/josefin-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/josefin-sans/500.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="What if I get it wrong? — a Salon Format learning experience for the first ten minutes of a first-aid course." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={`${base}brand/salon-format-mark.png`} />
    <title>What if I get it wrong? — Salon Format</title>
  </head>
  <body class="case-page first-aid-case">
    <header class="case-header">
      <a class="case-home" href="https://salonformat.com/" aria-label="Back to Salon Format home"><img src={`${base}brand/salon-format-mark.png`} alt="" /><span>Salon Format</span></a>
      <a href={`${base}#projects`}>All projects</a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="case-hero">
        <div class="case-hero-copy">
          <p class="project-status">Interactive learning experience · English / German</p>
          <h1>What if I<br /><em>get it wrong?</em></h1>
          <p class="case-deck">A short learning experience about the moment before practical training begins — and how a learner can move from uncertainty into participation.</p>
          <div class="case-actions">
            <a class="case-button" href="https://firstaid.salonformat.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the experience <span class="ui-arrow ui-arrow-external" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="first-aid-case-preview">
          <div class="experience-browser" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            <img src={`${base}images/first-aid/experience-preview.png`} alt="" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-intro">
        <p class="case-number">The learning problem</p>
        <h2>How can practical learning begin before someone feels fully confident?</h2>
        <p>The experience does not teach medical procedures. It focuses on a familiar barrier in practical courses: the fear of getting something wrong in front of others. The learner leaves with a concrete way to enter practice safely and deliberately.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="case-process first-aid-process">
        <div class="process-heading">
          <p class="case-number">Learning journey</p>
          <h2>Orient.<br />Choose.<br />Try.<br />Review.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="journey-list">
          <li><span>Orient</span><p>Make the sequence, format and available support visible.</p></li>
          <li><span>Choose a level</span><p>Select the smallest form of participation that still creates real practice.</p></li>
          <li><span>Try</span><p>Take one manageable attempt instead of waiting for complete confidence.</p></li>
          <li><span>Use feedback</span><p>Identify what worked and one specific action for the next attempt.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="decision-section first-aid-decisions">
        <p class="case-number">Key design decisions</p>
        <div class="decision-grid">
          <article><h3>Learning, not interpretation</h3><p>Flip cards introduce the model. Retrieval questions and scenarios then ask learners to recognise and apply it.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Clear right and wrong</h3><p>Feedback explains each choice, and progression remains locked until the learning goal has been met.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Professional calm</h3><p>Sage, warm white and precise red accents create a medical association without imitating clinical software.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Accessible entry</h3><p>English and German versions, optional voice-over, keyboard support and responsive layouts offer more than one way in.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-role first-aid-role">
        <p class="case-number">Role and contribution</p>
        <h2>Learning Experience Design · Concept · Writing · Learning Logic · Visual Direction · Interaction Design · Voice-over Direction · Prototyping</h2>
        <p>A self-initiated portfolio prototype exploring how learning design can support participation in professional training without claiming subject-matter expertise in medical procedures.</p>
      </section>

      <nav class="case-next" aria-label="Project navigation">
        <p>Next case study</p>
        <a href={`${base}projects/learning`}>Learning, Differently <span class="ui-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </nav>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
